  {
    "key": "francesca caccini",
    "name": "Francesca Caccini",
    "slots": {
      "origin": {
        "status": "gap",
        "facts": [
          {
            "f": "Francesca Caccini 1587 年 9 月 18 日生於佛羅倫斯，是作曲家 Giulio Caccini 的女兒，從小由父親教導音樂。",
            "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
            "src2": "https://www.historyhit.com/culture/francesca-caccini-operas-first-female-composer/",
            "from": "new"
          },
          {
            "f": "她除了音樂，還受過拉丁文、部分希臘文與現代語文、數學的人文教育。",
            "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
            "single": true,
            "from": "new"
          },
          {
            "f": "她少女時與妹妹 Settimia 一起隨父親的家庭歌唱團體演出，當時人稱 le donne di Giulio Romano，為梅第奇宮廷唱父親的作品。",
            "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
            "src2": "https://www.historyhit.com/culture/francesca-caccini-operas-first-female-composer/",
            "from": "new"
          },
          {
            "f": "她在梅第奇宮廷擔任教師、室內歌手、排練指導與作曲，到 1627 年初；1614 年起是宮廷薪資最高的樂師，佛羅倫斯人暱稱她 La Cecchina。",
            "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
            "src2": "https://www.historyhit.com/culture/francesca-caccini-operas-first-female-composer/",
            "from": "new"
          }
        ]
      },
      "sound": {
        "status": "gap",
        "facts": [
          {
            "f": "她 1618 年在佛羅倫斯出版《Il primo libro delle musiche》，收 36 首獨唱歌曲與女高音／低音二重唱，分宗教與世俗兩部分，是她作為佛羅倫斯新風格作曲家的主要文獻。",
            "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
            "src2": "https://imslp.org/wiki/Primo_Libro_delle_Musiche_(Caccini,_Francesca)",
            "from": "new"
          },
          {
            "f": "這本集子的曲目橫跨哀歌、拉丁文與義大利文的宗教歌，以及帶機智的分節歌；也被視為兼具教學用途，反映她作為教師的做法。",
            "src": "https://imslp.org/wiki/Primo_Libro_delle_Musiche_(Caccini,_Francesca)",
            "single": true,
            "from": "new"
          },
          {
            "f": "她的舞台音樂多為替詩人 Michelangelo Buonarroti the Younger 的喜劇所寫，例如《La Tancia》（1613）、《Il passatempo》（1614）與《La fiera》（1619），留存下來的極少。",
            "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
            "single": true,
            "from": "new"
          },
          {
            "f": "有評者稱她是「戲劇性和聲驚奇的大師」。",
            "src": "https://www.historyhit.com/culture/francesca-caccini-operas-first-female-composer/",
            "single": true,
            "from": "new"
          }
        ]
      },
      "legacy": {
        "status": "gap",
        "facts": [
          {
            "f": "她唯一留存的舞台作品《La liberazione di Ruggiero》（1625）普遍被視為現存最古老、由女性作曲家寫的歌劇。",
            "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
            "src2": "https://www.italyonthisday.com/search/label/Francesa%20Caccini",
            "from": "new"
          },
          {
            "f": "《La liberazione di Ruggiero》1625 年在佛羅倫斯郊外的 Poggio Imperiale 別墅，為來訪的波蘭王子 Ladislaus Sigismondo 首演；王子很滿意，1628 年要求在華沙再演一次。",
            "src": "https://www.italyonthisday.com/search/label/Francesa%20Caccini",
            "src2": "https://www.historyhit.com/culture/francesca-caccini-operas-first-female-composer/",
            "from": "new"
          }
        ]
      },
      "era": {
        "status": "gap",
        "facts": [
          {
            "f": "第一任丈夫 1626 年底過世後，她 1627 年改嫁盧卡貴族 Tommaso Raffaelli，1630 年再度喪偶，1634 年回到佛羅倫斯，替梅第奇宮廷的女性教學並寫室內樂；之後不再見於公開紀錄。",
            "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
            "src2": "https://www.historyhit.com/culture/francesca-caccini-operas-first-female-composer/",
            "from": "new"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "milestones": [
      {
        "f": "1618 年出版《Il primo libro delle musiche》，收 36 首獨唱與二重唱。",
        "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
        "src2": "https://imslp.org/wiki/Primo_Libro_delle_Musiche_(Caccini,_Francesca)",
        "from": "new"
      },
      {
        "f": "1625 年首演《La liberazione di Ruggiero》，被視為現存最古老的女性作曲歌劇。",
        "src": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesca_Caccini",
        "src2": "https://www.italyonthisday.com/search/label/Francesa%20Caccini",
        "from": "new"
      }
    ],
